post.description:
Works for both authenticated and anonymous users.
Body: { messageId?, chatId, type, reason?, comment?, modelSet? }
Anonymous-capable: a Bearer JWT, cm_access cookie, or ?token= is honored when present but not required (handlers may still self-check → 401).

POST /chats {title, folderId?, mode?}
Accepts a user JWT or a scoped `dgt_` agent token (scope enforced per-route).
Agent-token scope required: `chats:write`.

patch.description:
PATCH /chats/:id {title?, mode?, folderId?, archived?, systemPrompt?}
Accepts a user JWT or a scoped `dgt_` agent token (scope enforced per-route).
Agent-token scope required: `chats:write`.

